{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/HonClementJimbo/videos/at-independence-in-1960-nigeria-inherited-a-population-of-45-million-people-with/1050729530191005/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/HonClementJimbo/videos/at-independence-in-1960-nigeria-inherited-a-population-of-45-million-people-with/1050729530191005/","title":"1.1K views · 27 reactions | At Independence in 1960, Nigeria inherited a population of 45 million people with a corresponding Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of $4.2bn.\n\nFast forward to day after 65 years, the population of Nigeria has increased to over 200m people with an increment in GDP to over $450bn.\n\nQuestion?\n\nDoes the increase in the GDP reflected in the prosperity of an average Nigerian?\n\nThe answer is No\n\nHere is the reason, watch👇👇👇 | Clement Jimbo","description":"At Independence in 1960, Nigeria inherited a population of 45 million people with a corresponding Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of $4.2bn.\n\nFast forward to day after 65 years, the population of...","language":"en","text":"APPRECIATION MESSAGE FROM THE GOOD PEOPLE OF NTO OTOK COMMUNITY\nThe good people of Nto Otok Community sincerely express their profound appreciation to Hon. Clement Jimbo, the distinguished representative of Abak/Etim Ekpo/ Ika Federal Constituency in the Federal House of Representatives, for his remarkable commitment to the development and well-being of his constituents.\nWe are particularly grateful for your generous provision of 20 solar-powered street lights to Nto Otok Community. This laudable initiative will greatly improve security, visibility, and movement within our community, while also contributing to a safer and more vibrant environment for our people.\nYour consistent demonstration of quality leadership, compassion, and genuine service to humanity has not gone unnoticed. You have continued to show that true representation is about touching lives, empowering communities, and bringing meaningful development to the grassroots.\nHon. Clement Jimbo, we appreciate your good works and your unwavering dedication to the people. Nto Otok Community is proud to have a representative who listens, acts, and delivers.\nMay God continue to grant you wisdom, strength, and the capacity to do even greater things for our people and our constituency.\nThank you for your service. Thank you for your leadership. Thank you for remembering Nto Otok.\nLong live Hon. Clement Jimbo!\nLong live Abak/Etim Ekpo Federal/ Ika Constituency!\nLong live Nto Otok Community!\nSigned:\nNsidibe Udofa","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2123.1565050038625,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}